---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const privacyEmail = 'privacy@elysetindall.com';
const description =
  'Privacy policy for elysetindall.com, including contact forms, Studio CRM contacts, paid voice-lesson payments via Stripe, SMS inquiry alerts, and how to opt out of text messages.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description={description} hideFooterCta>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-gel">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl text-spotlight md:text-6xl">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
      How {site.name} ({site.url.replace(/^https:\/\//, '')}) collects and uses information on this
      site — including paid voice lessons, Stripe checkout, Studio CRM contacts, and SMS program
      details carriers may request. Last updated August 29, 2026.
    </p>

    <div class="prose-site mt-12">
      <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a professional portfolio and voice-lesson site for {site.name}. We collect only
        what we need to respond to casting and lesson inquiries, keep signed-in Studio teaching
        contacts, take payment for scheduled private voice lessons, run the site securely, and (in
        production) send short text alerts about inquiries to the studio’s designated phone number.
      </p>

      <h2 id="information-we-collect">Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Inquiry forms.</strong> Name, preferred contact method (defaults to email), email
          and/or phone as needed for that preference, optional organization, lesson format
          preference when applicable, and your message. Forms are protected with Cloudflare
          Turnstile.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical data.</strong> Standard web logs and application monitoring may record
          coarse request metadata (for example timestamps, status codes, and correlation IDs) to
          operate and troubleshoot the site. We do not sell personal information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics.</strong> On public pages we use Google Analytics 4 to understand
          aggregate traffic (for example pages viewed and approximate geography). The Measurement
          ID is configured as a site build setting. Private Studio pages are excluded. We do not
          use this data for advertising personalization on this site.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Student and parent sign-in.</strong> When contact accounts are enabled, students
          and parents may sign in with Google, Apple, or Microsoft through our identity provider
          (Microsoft Entra External ID) to book lessons or manage an account. We receive the name
          and email (or Apple Hide My Email relay) those providers share. Sign-in is optional —
          lesson and casting inquiries do not require an account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Studio CRM.</strong> When a signed-in Studio user adds a teaching or career
          contact, we store the name and optional email, phone, personas, notes, and related-person
          links in Azure Table Storage for that user’s Studio workspace. This is not a public
          directory and is not written into the website repository.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Lesson payments.</strong> When you pay for a private voice lesson, Stripe
          (a separate payment processor) collects the details needed to complete checkout and send
          a receipt — typically your name, email, and payment-method data. This site does not
          collect or store card numbers, bank account numbers, or wallet credentials. We receive
          payment confirmation from Stripe (amount, time, lesson length, and the email on the
          receipt) so we can match the payment to your lesson.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="how-we-use-information">How we use information</h2>
      <p>
        Contact details and messages from inquiry forms are used to reply about casting materials or
        private voice lessons via the contact method you prefer. Optional phone numbers you provide
        are for follow-up on that inquiry — not for unrelated marketing lists. We do not send
        promotional SMS campaigns to visitors. Studio CRM contacts are used only to operate the
        teaching business (schedule, notes, payment status, and transactional lesson email or SMS
        reminders when opted in). Payment
        information is used only to collect lesson fees, issue refunds when applicable, keep
        bookkeeping records, and prevent fraud.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sharing">Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Inquiry content is processed by our hosting, form-verification, and messaging providers so
        we can deliver and respond to your request. Analytics events from public pages are processed
        by Google Analytics. Signed-in Studio CRM records are stored in Azure Table Storage in the
        same hosting environment as the site. Lesson payments are processed by Stripe; Stripe acts as an independent
        controller of the payment data it collects. See Stripe’s privacy policy at{' '}
        <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          stripe.com/privacy</a
        >. We do not sell or rent your information. We may disclose information if required by law.
      </p>

      <h2 id="payments">Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Paid offerings on this site are <strong>private voice lessons</strong> only (vocal pedagogy,
        vocal health, and contemporary commercial music). The site does not sell acting lessons.
        Checkout happens on Stripe-hosted Payment Links. Card and wallet data never touch our
        servers. After you pay, Stripe may email you a receipt; we may also see the email address
        you enter at checkout so we can confirm you are paid for the scheduled session.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you need a payment record corrected or deleted where the law allows, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>. Some payment records must be kept
        for tax and bookkeeping obligations even after a lesson is complete.
      </p>

      <h2 id="studio-crm">Studio CRM</h2>
      <p>
        Studio is a login-protected workspace. Contacts saved there (inquiry follow-up, voice-lesson
        students, parents, representation, and casting relationships) are visible only to the
        signed-in Studio user who owns them. Stripe checkout emails may be matched to a Studio
        contact so lesson lifetime value can be shown; unmatched payments stay listed for the
        operator to attach. Operational logs and application monitoring record contact identifiers
        and error kinds — not email addresses, phone numbers, or note bodies. Monthly operations
        summaries count inquiry volume only and do not include CRM names.
      </p>
      <p>
        To request correction or deletion of a Studio CRM record where the law allows, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sms">SMS notifications</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Program:</strong> When someone submits a casting or lesson inquiry on this website,
        the site may send a short transactional text message to the studio’s designated mobile
        number so {site.name} can respond promptly. These are business inquiry alerts, not
        consumer marketing blasts.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Message frequency:</strong> Varies with how often forms are submitted (typically
        low volume). Message and data rates may apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Consent:</strong> By operating and configuring this SMS alert number for the
        studio, the message recipient consents to receive these transactional inquiry texts.
        Visitors who submit a form consent to being contacted about that inquiry via their preferred
        method (email or phone), as described above. Submitting a form does not enroll you in
        marketing texts.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Opt out:</strong> Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to any SMS from our messaging number
        to cancel further texts to that phone. After you opt out, you will receive a confirmation
        and we will stop sending SMS alerts to that number. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for help,
        or email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages. Supported carriers in the
        United States typically include major nationwide providers; availability may vary.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Public link for this section (for carrier / toll-free verification forms):{' '}
        <a href={`${site.url}/privacy#sms`}>{site.url}/privacy#sms</a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">Retention</h2>
      <p>
        Inquiry messages and related operational logs are kept only as long as needed to respond and
        run the site securely, unless a longer period is required by law. Studio CRM contacts are
        kept until the Studio user archives or deletes them, or asks us to remove them where the
        law allows. Payment and refund records are kept as long as needed for taxes, bookkeeping,
        and dispute handling. Stripe retains payment-method data according to its own policies.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions:{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>
        {' · '}
        <a href="/contact">Contact forms</a>
        {' · '}
        <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(.prose-site h2) {
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }
</style>
